### Bound shutdown when WMI is unavailable

**Severity:** `high`

`WBEM_FLAG_CONNECT_USE_MAX_WAIT` can still block a synchronous `ConnectServer` call long enough for `Stop()` to wait on the observer thread during service shutdown or mode changes. This can make disabling Follow Brightness or stopping the service exceed expected shutdown timing when WMI is unavailable. Keep the worker state alive independently and bound `Stop()` so shutdown can continue after cancellation is requested.

```suggestion
    void Stop()
    {
        _state->stop = true;
        if (_thread.joinable())
        {
            auto done = _state->done.get_future();
            if (done.wait_for(std::chrono::seconds(2)) == std::future_status::ready)
            {
                _thread.join();
            }
            else
            {
                _thread.detach();
            }
        }
    }
```

### Use a deterministic value when multiple built-in panels report brightness

**Severity:** `medium`

`WmiMonitorBrightness` can expose more than one active internal panel, but the current code reads only the first row from an unordered WMI result set. On dual-panel devices the selected brightness source can be arbitrary and can ignore changes on the other panel. Enumerate the active rows and apply a documented deterministic policy; this suggestion uses the maximum reported brightness so bright outdoor conditions on any built-in panel keep the theme in light mode.

```suggestion
                    IWbemClassObject* pObj = nullptr;
                    ULONG returned = 0;
                    std::optional<int> maxBrightness;
                    while (!state->stop &&
                           pEnum->Next(kNextTimeoutMs, 1, &pObj, &returned) == WBEM_S_NO_ERROR &&
                           returned)
                    {
                        VARIANT vt;
                        VariantInit(&vt);
                        if (SUCCEEDED(pObj->Get(L"CurrentBrightness", 0, &vt, nullptr, nullptr)))
                        {
                            int brightness = static_cast<int>(vt.bVal);
                            maxBrightness = maxBrightness && *maxBrightness > brightness ? *maxBrightness : brightness;
                        }
                        VariantClear(&vt);
                        pObj->Release();
                        pObj = nullptr;
                    }
```

### Invalidate cached brightness when no active panel is reported

**Severity:** `medium`

When a successful WMI query returns no active brightness rows, the previous brightness remains cached indefinitely. Later settings changes or external-theme checks can then act on a disconnected panel's stale value instead of entering the existing unknown-brightness path. Reset both observer and manager state with a sentinel and avoid treating that invalidation as a threshold crossing.

```suggestion
                    else if (!state->stop && !maxBrightness && lastBrightness != -1)
                    {
                        lastBrightness = -1;
                        try
                        {
                            state->callback(lastBrightness);
                        }
                        catch (...) {}
                    }
```
